  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member who uses HFR on iOS and on Android, I want my allowlist (and later my super-favourites) to follow my HFR account across apps, so that I set them once. Operator decision 2026-10-28 (ADR 0013 draft, Q3): for now the allowlist is stored in iCloud KVS; a shared MPStorage namespace is specified and ported with the Android app's maintainers.\n\nScope\n- Draft a namespace contract for the shared MPStorage document: name, JSON schema, size budget, merge rules, versioning. Base it on the existing namespaces (blacklist, bookmarks, `superFavs` and `lastRead` from the userscripts, #272).\n- Port: once the contract is agreed, SwiftHFR reads and writes the namespace and migrates the iCloud copy into it.\n- Never write a new namespace into users' documents before the contract is agreed (ADR 0013).\n\nBlocked by\n- #272: capture of a non-empty MPStorage document.\n- Contact with the Android app's maintainer. This is a message outside GitHub, so it needs the operator's go (AGENTS.md §0).\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md (MPStorage) documents the contract, with a link to the other app's agreement.\n- A lot row is added to docs/LOTS.md for the port.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- #272\n- Contact with the Android app's maintainer: a message outside GitHub, on the operator's go (AGENTS.md §0)\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
